We introduce a groundbreaking approach to category-level perception, enabling precise determination of object geometry and location from semantic keypoints in both two and three dimensions. Our method, built on a novel neural network, can function optimally even when data is incomplete or compromised, and we demonstrate its effectiveness through rigorous testing on two challenging datasets. Furthermore, our research reveals that reliable 3D pose estimation is achievable even in the absence of depth information, and we also present a dataset specifically designed for evaluating the resilience of category-level perception models. Our code and dataset are now available for public access. 

